    "normalization": [
      "A workspace command loses each source flag and its value: --file, --git-dir, --repository, --commit, --git-path. A publish also loses --body when its redacted value is the digest its entry records for the text, so the text is still compared through that digest.",
      "An adapter session loses --git-dir and --repository with their values.",
      "An action loses wall_ms (timing) and sources (how many source locators a capture showed).",
      "A public key generated for the run becomes public-key:OWNER, the institution or actor named in the command that introduced it; the first owner named wins, so a key reused for another owner still differs, and a key no command introduced stays as it is.",
      "A workspace context id, derived from a random name in its open request, becomes context:ARTIFACT, the artifact published from it, or context:unpublished.",
      "A signed envelope {body, signature} keeps its body; its signature bytes become <signature>.",
      "Receipts and contexts are compared as multisets because the store orders them by random ids; every other table and the action list keep their order.",
      "The source_locators table is left out and reported separately; it holds the source locators.",
      "Stored JSON columns are parsed once; nothing else is dropped or rewritten."
    ]
  },
